    {
      "description": "Single catch-all for anything that doesn't get a typed\nvariant: generic emits (`Items<T>`, `Value<V>`),\napi/call.rs passthrough (`Resp`, `Chunk`), and raw\n`serde_json::Value`. The map's keys flatten directly\nalongside `kind` — there is no inner field wrapping.\n\nConstruct via [`NotificationValue::other`]. The payload\nmust serialize to a JSON object (so its entries can sit at\nthe same level as `kind`), and its keys cannot include\n`\"kind\"` (would collide with the discriminator).\n\nWire examples:\n  `{\"kind\":\"other\",\"items\":[…]}`        (Items<T>)\n  `{\"kind\":\"other\",\"value\":<V>}`        (Value<V>)",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "kind": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "other"
          ]
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": true
    }
